---
// One of the app's own labels, named on a page (U5, KTD8, R11): set in Fragment Mono like
// a key, so a reader can find the control by its name. Pages use it without importing it
// ([...slug].astro hands it to every page). Write the label exactly as the app shows it;
// site/tests/content.test.ts fails when the app no longer shows it.
//
// A templated label escapes its placeholder's braces in the page (`Pull \{agent\}'s
// handoff`), so MDX keeps them as text. The placeholder renders as text, braces and all,
// in a <var> that reads as the part the app fills in. Styles live in styles/guide.css.

const html = await Astro.slots.render("default");
// The slot is MDX's own output: text, with any `{name}` placeholder left as braces. The
// guide's typography curls quotes, but the app's labels use straight ones, so a label
// shows them straight, as on screen.
const label = html
  .trim()
  .replace(/[‘’]/g, "'")
  .replace(/[“”]/g, '"')
  .replace(/\{([^{}<>]+)\}/g, '<var class="guide-ui-slot">{$1}</var>');
---

<kbd class="guide-ui" set:html={label} />
